[Event "Intermediate tactics: deflection, the lesson"]
[Result "1-0"]
[Role "teaching"]
[Variant "Standard"]
[ChapterURL "https://lichess.org/study/cB9DXF3Y/eBDFn8CO"]
[FEN "r1q3k1/4bppp/pp2pn2/4B3/8/2N2Q2/PPPR1PPP/6K1 b - - 0 18"]
[SetUp "1"]
[Site "https://lichess.org/analysis/r1q3k1/4bppp/pp2pn2/4B3/8/2N2Q2/PPPR1PPP/6K1_b_-_-_0_18"]

{ Welcome to intermediate tactics. First trick: deflection. Pull a defender off its post, and whatever it was guarding falls. }
18... Nd7 { His knight drops to d7. Now only his queen on c8 guards the rook on a8. Take the knight with your rook and make her choose. [%cal Yd2d7,Rc8a8] } 19. Rxd7 { The rook grabs the knight. If his queen takes back, she leaves c8, and the rook on a8 has no guard. [%cal Rc8a8] } (19. Bd4 { A nice square, but it does nothing to his queen, and she keeps guarding the rook on a8. } 19... Bf6 20. h3 h6 21. a4 Bxd4 22. Rxd4 { The bishops come off, his queen never left c8, and the game is level. The deflection chance is gone. }) (19. Bd6 { Trading bishops never touches his queen, so she keeps guarding the rook on a8. } 19... Bxd6 20. Rxd6 Rb8 21. Qe4 Qc7 { Level: his rook left a8 for b8, and every piece of his is guarded. }) 19... Qxd7 { His queen takes back. She has left c8, and nothing guards the rook on a8 now. Take it with check. [%csl Ra8][%cal Yf3a8] } 20. Qxa8+ { Check, and the rook is yours. You gave a rook for his knight and took a rook back: a knight up. That is deflection. } (20. Bxg7 { The pawn on g7 is small change, and it gives his rook time to leave the corner. } 20... Rd8 21. Bh6 Qd4 22. g3 Qf6 { His rook escaped to d8. You gave a rook for a knight, one pawn does not pay for it, and he is better. }) (20. h4 { A quiet pawn move lets his rook walk out of the corner. } 20... Rd8 21. a3 f6 22. Bf4 b5 { The rook got out to d8, you are still down the rook you gave for his knight, and he is winning. }) 1-0


[Event "Intermediate tactics: deflection with a check"]
[Result "0-1"]
[Role "exercise"]
[Variant "Standard"]
[ChapterURL "https://lichess.org/study/cB9DXF3Y/h5xEA1B2"]
[FEN "2r3k1/p4ppp/3r1n2/2b3B1/Q7/6P1/PPB1qP1P/R4RK1 w - - 7 24"]
[SetUp "1"]
[Site "https://lichess.org/analysis/2r3k1/p4ppp/3r1n2/2b3B1/Q7/6P1/PPB1qP1P/R4RK1_w_-_-_7_24"]

{ Your queen has reached e2, deep in his camp, and your bishop on c5 aims at his king side. }
24. Rae1 { His rook comes to e1 and attacks your queen. His other rook, on f1, now has two jobs. Find the deflection. } 24... Bxf2+ { The bishop gives itself up on f2 with check. King moves lose even more, so his rook on f1 has to take it. } (24... Qh5 { The queen retreats, and his rooks keep both e1 and f2 covered. } 25. Re5 Bd4 26. Rf5 Qh3 { His rooks are active, your queen is pushed around, and he is better. }) (24... Qf3 { The queen stays active, but his bishop comes to e3 and blocks yours. } 25. Be3 Bxe3 26. Rxe3 Qb7 { The bishops are gone, his rook on e3 guards everything, and he is better. }) (24... Qg4 { This offers the queens off, and without her your attack on e1 is gone. } 25. Qxg4 Nxg4 26. Bf5 Nxf2 { Your knight took f2, but his bishop on f5 attacks your rook on c8 and he is winning. [%cal Rf5c8] }) 25. Rxf2 { His rook takes on f2. Look at what it used to guard. } 25... Qxe1+ { Check, and his rook on e1 is yours. The rook on f1 left to take your bishop, so nothing guarded e1: a rook for a bishop. That is deflection. } (25... Qxf2+ { This takes the wrong rook: his king stands right beside f2. } 26. Kxf2 h6 27. Bf5 Rf8 { You gave your queen and bishop for one rook, and you are lost. }) (25... Qa6 { The queen runs, but you gave a bishop and took nothing back. } 26. Bxf6 Qxa4 27. Bxa4 gxf6 { The queens are off and you are a whole piece down. He is winning. }) 0-1


