[FEN "rn1qkb1r/5pp1/p1ppb2p/3N4/2pQP3/7P/PPPN1PP1/R1B1K2R w KQkq - 0 12"]
[SetUp "1"]
[Site "https://lichess.org/analysis/rn1qkb1r/5pp1/p1ppb2p/3N4/2pQP3/7P/PPPN1PP1/R1B1K2R_w_KQkq_-_0_12"]

{ His knight on d5 has jumped deep into your camp, and his queen on d4 stands behind it. }
12. Nb6 { His knight jumps to b6 and attacks your rook on a8. His queen on d4 is its only guard. } 12... c5 { Your pawn steps to c5 and attacks his queen. It also stands on the diagonal from d4 to b6, cutting her off from the knight. [%cal Rd4b6] } (12... Ra7 { The rook dodges, but his knight on b6 stays guarded. } 13. Nd5 Rb7 14. Nf4 Qf6 { His knight got back out to f4, and he is better. }) (12... Nd7 { This leaves your rook on a8 to the knight. } 13. Nxa8 Qxa8 14. Nxc4 d5 { You lost a rook for a knight and the c4 pawn. He is winning. }) (12... d5 { The wrong pawn: it does not touch the line from d4 to b6. } 13. Nxa8 Nd7 14. O-O Qxa8 { You won his knight back, but he is the exchange up. }) 13. Qe3 { His queen steps back to e3. Your pawn on c5 still blocks her way to b6. } 13... Qxb6 { A free knight. Your pawn on c5 stood between his queen and b6: that is interference. } (13... Ra7 { The rook dodges, and his knight on b6 hops out with a pawn. } 14. Nbxc4 Nc6 15. Qg3 Nd4 { His knight escaped to c4, and he is a little better. }) (13... Nc6 { Your rook on a8 is still attacked, and his knight takes it. } 14. Nxa8 Nd4 15. Kd1 Be7 { His knight on a8 is stuck and you will win it, but you stay the exchange down. }) 0-1


[Event "Intermediate tactics: interference on the rank"]
